  "result": "I fixed two bugs in `src/`, and `npm test` now passes all 243 tests (2 were failing before). I didn't touch the tests.\n\n1. **`src/cart.js`: tax was applied before the discount.** `total()` added tax to the subtotal first and then took the discount off, even though its own comment says the discount comes off the pre-tax subtotal. I swapped the order so the discount comes off first and tax is added to what's left. With 100 of items, a fixed 20 discount and 10% tax, the total is now 88 instead of 90.\n2. **`src/discount.js`: a fixed discount could make the total negative.** A fixed discount bigger than the subtotal gave a negative amount (-14.5 in the test). It now stops at zero, using `Math.max(0, amount - discount.value)`.\n\nPercentage discounts were already correct. The swap only changes their results when the discount and tax are both nonzero, and then only in the floating-point rounding, which the totals round away.",
